// Q-049 `http.get`'s options take only redirects, public_only and cache: `{ timeout: 2 }` is ignored without a word (by `quillo check` and at run time), and a call cannot be made to give up sooner than Quillo's own 10 s to connect and 60 s in all
// mode: check
// open-when: /ok \(0 routes/
// fixed-when: timeout
// From FEEDBACK5.md (found on ae6a6e5). In app/stays, Overpass (places around a stay) answered in 34 s:
// `http.get(url, headers, { timeout: 5 })` waited the 34 s all the same (an 8 s httpbin delay with
// timeout: 2 took 8.3 s). src/fetch.rs reads only "redirects", "public_only" and "cache"; the 10 s
// and 60 s limits are not in the guide. The app asks for the slow services after the page shows,
// and falls back to Photon only when Overpass fails outright.

fn places(url: str) with http = http.get(url, { "User-Agent": "repro/1" }, { timeout: 2, public_only: true })
